<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Ausci</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.) · capital Elimberris</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Aquitanian people of Gascony whose chief town Elimberris became Auch, later the religious capital of the region.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Ausci lived in the hills of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a>, in the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gers">Gers</a>. They were among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquitani">Aquitani</a>, whose language was related to Basque; the name of their town, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auch">Elimberris</a>, is usually read as Basque-like 'new town', comparable with Iliberris in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomponius-mela">Pomponius Mela</a> calls them the most distinguished of the Aquitanian peoples. Nothing is recorded of their rulers before the conquest.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Ausci gave hostages to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/publius-licinius-crassus">Publius Crassus</a> in 56 BCE without fighting. Their town was refounded as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auch">Augusta Auscorum</a>, and in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it replaced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eauze">Eauze</a> as the metropolitan see of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novempopulania">Novempopulana</a>. Auch remained the seat of an archbishop for all of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ausci.jpg" alt="Ausci" width="320" height="274"><figcaption>Image: Sémhur · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aquitani_tribes_map-fr.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Elimberris</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Aquitanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>France</dd></dl></aside></div>

